{
  "prompt": "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The scene features two rustic, wide-rimmed matte ceramic bowls of smoky tempeh, white bean, and kale soup, centered in the frame with generous negative space. The camera is at a 3/4 overhead angle to show the vibrant contents of both bowls clearly, with the primary bowl sharp in the foreground and the second bowl softly blurred behind it. Shallow depth of field creates a beautiful natural bokeh. Soft, natural light enters from a window on the left, casting subtle, gentle shadows and highlighting the sheen of olive oil droplets on the broth surface. The setting is an aged oak wood table with visible grain and natural wear. Props include a tarnished silver soup spoon resting casually beside the front bowl, a rumpled, off-white linen napkin tucked slightly under one side, and a few stray, bright green kale fragments scattered naturally on the wood. The soup itself is a rich, warm mosaic: tender, dark green kale ribbons, plump pearly white cannellini beans, and golden-brown, crumbled tempeh bits with a subtle smoky paprika-infused crust, all swimming in a savory, translucent broth tinted with the deep red of diced tomatoes. The dish looks hearty and steam-softened, with the ingredients clearly visible and identifiable. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene captures a home-cooked meal, warm, authentic, and lived-in. Includes slight natural imperfections: an asymmetric garnish, a tiny broth droplet on the bowl's rim, and a stray grain of smoked paprika on the table. Warm, golden-hour color temperature, cozy and inviting. No text, no watermark, no logo, no hands, no faces. Indistinguishable from a professional cookbook photograph."
}
